.TH SLIDEWIRE 1 "2026-10-11" "Slidewire 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slidewire \- control app and device volumes with a MIDI controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slidewire
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B slidewire
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARGS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Slidewire turns a MIDI controller into a volume mixer: faders set the volume of
apps and audio devices, buttons mute and switch them, and the controller's LEDs
show the state. It works with PipeWire and PulseAudio.
.PP
Started without a command it opens its window, or brings up the window of the
copy that is already running.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-minimized
Start in the tray without opening the window.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-ports
List MIDI ports and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-monitor " [\fIPATTERN\fR]"
Print incoming MIDI messages, from ports whose name contains \fIPATTERN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-doctor " [\fIPATTERN\fR]"
Check why a controller doesn't show up: USB, sound driver, ALSA sequencer,
kernel updates, and whether Slidewire could open it. Default: nanoKONTROL2.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-icon
Install a menu entry and icons for the current user (for builds without a package).
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove what \fB\-\-install\-icon\fR and autostart added. Settings are kept.
.TP
.BR \-\-write\-icons " \fIDIR\fR"
Write the app icons for the hicolor theme under \fIDIR\fR (for packaging).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help.
.SH COMMANDS
These control the running app, for scripts and keyboard shortcuts.
\fISTRIP\fR is a strip name such as "Knob 3", or a number for that fader.
.TP
.B strips
List the strips with their volume and what they control.
.TP
.BR set " \fISTRIP\fR \fIPERCENT\fR|+\fIN\fR|\-\fIN\fR"
Set a strip's volume, or change it by \fIN\fR percent.
.TP
.BR mute " \fISTRIP\fR [on|off|toggle]"
Mute or unmute a strip. Default: toggle.
.TP
.BR bank " \fIN\fR"
Switch to bank \fIN\fR (1 is the first).
.TP
.BR scene " \fINAME\fR"
Recall a saved scene.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/slidewire/settings.json
Settings. The previous version is kept as \fIsettings.json.bak\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/slidewire/profiles/*.json
Controller profiles, in the format of MIDI Mixer for Windows plus Slidewire's own fields.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/slidewire/crash.log
Reports of crashes.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SLIDEWIRE_CONFIG
Use another configuration directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
slidewire set 1 +5          # fader 1 up by 5%
slidewire mute "Knob 2"     # toggle mute on knob 2
slidewire scene Gaming      # recall the scene "Gaming"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pactl (1),
.BR aconnect (1)
.PP
https://git.briggen.dev/NilsBriggen/SlideWire
